From e10fb08d37e6549106229705940dd21849f4420c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jawad Amin <jawadamin@google.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:28:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] [Quantization] Claim every DeepSeek V4 family model type
 for deepseek_v4_fp8

register_quantization_config lets this config override the quantization
method a checkpoint declares, and on TPU this class wins the
"deepseek_v4_fp8" name. It inherited a test that accepts only the model
type "deepseek_v4". The model types "deepseek_v4_text", "deepseek_v41"
and "deepseek_v41_text" therefore fell through to plain FP8.

A checkpoint that falls through gets VllmFp8MoEMethod for its experts.
That method cannot read packed E2M1 pairs, so the int8 expert lever
never runs. TPU v6e has no FP4 MXU, and the lever is the only path that
serves these checkpoints. Nothing raises, and nothing warns above debug
level, so the failure appears later as wrong output or a shape error.

Override override_quantization_method in this class. Ask the base class
first, so the AMD-Quark MXFP4 branch keeps its answer, then widen to the
three model types the base class misses.

Add tests/layers/vllm/test_deepseek_v4_fp8_config.py with 10 cases. Nine
hold the resolution for each model type and each rejection case. One
asserts that this class owns the registered name.

Signed-off-by: Jawad Amin <jawadamin@google.com>
